        "label": "Parts of the microsporangium",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Two parts",
        "lines": [
          "A mature microsporangium consists of two",
          "parts:",
          "1. the microsporangial wall, and",
          "2. the sporogenous tissue inside it.",
          "The wall has four layers. From outside in:",
          "epidermis, endothecium, middle layers,",
          "tapetum."
        ],
        "why": "Wall outside, sporogenous tissue inside — naming the two parts and listing the four wall layers in their outside-to-inside order sets up every later step.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Listing the layers in a scrambled order. The order IS the anatomy — outermost to innermost.",
          "Forgetting the sporogenous tissue — the wall exists to protect and feed it."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "'External Environment Makes Trouble': Epidermis, Endothecium, Middle layers, Tapetum — outside to inside.",
        "margin_note": "Two parts plus the ordered four-layer list — the frame for the whole answer."
