        "why": "The enlarged sector is the drawing that scores: four concentric layers in the right order with the microspore mother cells inside. The whole four-lobed anther outline adds time, not marks.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Swapping the tapetum and the endothecium. Tapetum is the INNERMOST layer, touching the sporogenous tissue.",
          "Drawing all layers the same thickness — the middle layers are the thin ones.",
          "Leaving out the microspore mother cells the wall surrounds."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw four arcs outside-in — big cells, fibrous cells, thin lines, fat feeding cells — then dot the mother cells below.",
        "margin_note": "Four labelled layers + microspore mother cells; 4-5 minutes with labels."
